<BaseLayout title="Fourth Wing Dragon Name Generator — Original Fantasy Names" description="Generate original fantasy dragon names from 600 combinations of invented syllables and Scottish Gaelic roots, with meanings and a copy button." breadcrumbs={[{name:'Name Generator',href:'/dragon-name-generator/'}]}>
<h1>Fourth Wing Dragon Name Generator</h1><p class="lead">Create an original fantasy name inspired by the sound of Scottish Gaelic roots. These are fan creations, not names from the novels.</p><NameGenerator/><section class="prose"><h2>How this generator works</h2><p>Each click chooses an invented prefix, a dictionary root and an invented suffix. Ten prefixes, six roots and ten suffixes make 600 distinct combinations. The displayed meaning belongs to the individual root. Combining syllables does not create a grammatical Gaelic translation.</p><p>The generator uses your browser’s random-number source and sends no name requests to a server. It avoids repeating the immediately previous result. Copy a favorite for personal notes or a creative project; check for existing uses before publication.</p><h2>Choosing a name for a character</h2><p>Start with the sound you want to hear. Shorter results can work as quick labels in notes, while longer results can suit a fantasy character, a game profile or a private writing exercise. Read the generated name aloud once or twice and look at the root shown beneath it. The root meaning is a prompt for atmosphere, not a definition of the complete compound.</p><p>Try several results before settling on one. The button uses a browser random source, so refreshing the page does not create a fixed sequence. The current result remains visible until you generate another name. The copy action places only the displayed name on your clipboard when you select it; no result is uploaded or saved by this site.</p><h2>What the root glossary means</h2><p>The glossary lists six Scottish Gaelic dictionary headwords and a short English meaning for each. A dictionary entry describes that single word. The invented prefix and suffix are sound elements created for this tool, so the combined output should be read as an original fantasy construction. It should not be presented as a translation, a traditional Gaelic name or a statement about the Empyrean books.</p><p>If you plan to publish a character or project using a generated result, search for existing uses and ask a fluent speaker to review any language claim. A familiar-looking syllable can occur in another name by chance. Treat the generator as a creative starting point, then make your own editorial decisions about spelling, pronunciation and context.</p><h2>Explore the wider site</h2><p>Use the <a href="/dragons/">dragon color and tail index</a> when you need a compact vocabulary list, or take the <a href="/quiz/dragon-type/">dragon quiz</a> for an original personality activity. The <a href="/guide-to-dragonkind/">Dragonkind guide</a> explains how this site separates source material from fan-made tools. You can return to this page at any time and generate another name without an account.</p></section>
</BaseLayout>
